[17592186280222 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280222 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280222 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b942317b-4cdd-5133-86a0-72edd836c45d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280432 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280432 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280432 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d0f00225-d1b5-51c3-b4d3-577d7c1a4eb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280786 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280786 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280786 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f9f4d654-5df4-51ef-9432-ac240b22f91a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186278996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281223 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dfb66dd7-ab41-588b-830e-54e330e9a934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281228 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e308b1a0-ff07-540c-b063-07bba0eb3e55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281683 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281683 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281683 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281683 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{24}$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{3}{8}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{5}{8}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=-2)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281683 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2b24b5d8-591a-5107-953f-3194f9f2c074" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281683 #edb/ref 1074 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=-2)=f(0,-2)=\\frac{1}{4}.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2) & =\\frac{5}{12}=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,-2) & =\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,2) & =\\frac{5}{24}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186383377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383376 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1aa5d990-d2c9-53e1-986d-feac4f9aa275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921